       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, twice the usual maximum for an adult. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use. A dose that high greatly raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Common regimens include:\n- 400\u2013800 mg by mouth three or four times daily, not to exceed 3,200 mg/day\n- 1600 mg total per day, for example 400 mg four times daily\n\nAlso, orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be confirmed by one. If a clinician on the medicine service confirms the intended dose, or you send me a corrected order, I'll enter it right away."
